# shell: desktop
# prefs: factory
# board: discover
# The board is found by its name on the bus, not by a port the harness
# hands over -- and finding it is not taking it in.  The desktop scans,
# offers what answered under the port it is on, and the board becomes
# ours when the Devices menu CONNECTS it; its window comes up then.  A
# native-USB console enumerates under its own name, which is what the
# scan matches.  The click brings that window to the front of the
# fixture's, as boarddraw does, before its title is asked.
wait 200
note nothing is mounted by merely being found: the first board on offer
note is taken in from the Devices menu, at the end of the bar
click 264 8
wait 10
menu-pick Connect to
wait 300
note and the board taken in has its window on the desktop
click 558 174
wait 20
expect-title Board window
